<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      strategy_defaults.opposite_side: whether the EOD detector writes this
      strategy's generated config for the OPPOSITE leg of the one the trend was
      detected on.

      Why it exists
      =============
      The detector scans the ATM CE and PE for a downtrend and, until now, always
      generated the config for the leg it detected on - the right shape for the
      sell-side strategies (PE downtrending -> sell the PE tomorrow). Strategy 3
      is the mirror trade: the day the PE ends downtrending (index rising) is the
      day it wants a CE BUY config, so that at the market moment strategy 1 sells
      the PE, strategy 3 buys the CE (see STRATEGIES.md, "Strategy 3").
      Strategy 4 by contrast buys the very leg the downtrend was detected on, so
      it keeps opposite_side = FALSE.

      Which side a strategy's generated config trades decides what trades get
      taken, so per CLAUDE.md #9 it is a strategy_defaults column, not code.

      Defaulted FALSE so every existing row - and any inserted without naming the
      column - keeps the detected-side behaviour unchanged.

      The column joins configSignature(): a flipped and an unflipped strategy
      must never share one generated config row, whatever the rest of their
      blocks say.
    -->
    <changeSet id="040_add_opposite_side_to_strategy_defaults" author="moneymaker">
        <addColumn tableName="strategy_defaults">
            <column name="opposite_side" type="BOOLEAN" defaultValueBoolean="false">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </addColumn>
    </changeSet>

    <!--
      Strategy 3 IS the mirror strategy - opposite_side = TRUE is its identity,
      not a tunable, so it is stamped declaratively rather than left to whoever
      types the INSERT. A no-op when the row does not exist yet (fresh database,
      or the strategy_defaults row for 3 not inserted): anyone adding that row
      after this changeset has run must set opposite_side = TRUE themselves -
      see the strategy_defaults section of docs/EOD_DOWNTREND.md.
    -->
    <changeSet id="040_mark_strategy3_opposite_side" author="moneymaker">
        <update tableName="strategy_defaults">
            <column name="opposite_side" valueBoolean="true"/>
            <where>strategy_id = 3</where>
        </update>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
